  "leangap": { deadline: null, blurb: "Four-week summer accelerator where high schoolers build a startup, launch to real customers and pitch investors. Runs online (June 14 to July 9, 2027) or in San Francisco at UC Berkeley with housing and meals (July 11 to August 7). Tuition is $6,450 online and $14,950 in person, with need-based scholarships.", location: "San Francisco, California, USA", format: "Hybrid", evidence: "Official page, checked 2026-09-25: \"Build a real startup, launch for real customers, and pitch to actual investors.\" Two four-week tracks are offered, \"Online\" and \"San Francisco (hosted at UC Berkeley)\" - the stored Boston location appears nowhere on the site. Tuition is \"$6,450 USD\" online and \"$14,950 USD\" in San Francisco including housing and meals, with need-based scholarships of 10-80% off online and 10-50% off in person. 2027 dates: online June 14 - July 9, San Francisco July 11 - August 7. No application deadline is posted. | Sept 15: 2026-04-30 was a past cycle's deadline and the official page (checked 2026-09-15) posts no later date." },
  "lumiere": { deadline: null, blurb: "Independent online research mentorship with PhD scholars from top universities, ending in an independent research paper. Lumiere admits several cohorts through the year rather than on one annual deadline, so check the application page for the cohort currently open.", evidence: "Official application page, checked 2026-09-28: it still advertises only 'Our Fall II Cohort Admission Deadline is September 27', which has passed, and no date is posted for the next cohort. The stored 2026-09-27 deadline was therefore being shipped as current after it expired. Cleared rather than replaced with a guess: Lumiere runs rolling cohorts and publishes each deadline as that cohort opens. | Sept 15: Official page: 'Our Fall II Cohort Admission Deadline is September 27'." },
  "mad-artslife": { deadline: "2027-01-03", verified: true, evidence: "Official page fetched and corroborated 2026-09-26 (HTTP 200). Eligibility wording on the page: 'Artslife Artslife is a paid summer internship for 10 rising sophomores and juniors in New York City public and charter high schools.'. The page also describes the programme: 'Teen Programs | Museum of Arts and Design Pay What You Wish on the first Wednesday of every month! Learn more .'. 100% of the listing's title terms and 100% of its organisation terms appear in the page text. This confirms the link resolves to a live page about this programme that is open to high schoolers. It is not a field-by-field audit of cost, grades or dates. | Earlier this run: Official page, checked 2026-09-22: Application Deadline: Sunday, January 3, 2027, at 11:59 PM. Each student who successfully completes the program will receive a $200 stipend and will be eligible for membership in MAD's Teen Council. | Sept 15: Official page: 'The application portal for the Artslife summer 2026 internship is now closed.' The January 3, 2027 date on that page belongs to the RECESS winter programme." },
  "manhattan-school": { deadline: null, blurb: "Saturday conservatory at Manhattan School of Music running through the academic year, in either Classical or Jazz Arts, for musicians aged 8 to 18. Students take a private lesson plus theory, ear training, composition, orchestra, chorus and conducting, and perform regularly. Entry is by audition.", category: "Fellowship", evidence: "Official page, checked 2026-09-25: the Precollege serves \"talented musicians aged 8 to 18\" in either the Classical or Jazz Arts programme, and \"Classes meet on Saturdays throughout the school year\" with private lessons plus theory, ear training, composition, orchestra, chorus and conducting. Category corrected from Summer Program: this runs across the academic year on Saturdays, not over the summer. The posted audition deadline, March 1, 2026, was for the 2026-27 year and has passed; no 2027-28 date is posted yet. | Sept 15: 2025-12-01 was a past cycle's deadline and the official page (checked 2026-09-15) posts no later date." },
  "mcdonalds-hacer": { deadline: null, verified: true, evidence: "Official page corroborated 2026-09-26. The listed page did not state who the programme is for, so its own eligibility page was followed to https://www.mcdonalds.com/us/en-us/community/hacer/eligibility-and-requirements.html, which states: 'eligible? Check out the requirements below to find out if the McDonald’s® HACER® National Scholarship is right for you: You’re a high school senior Must be a legal U.S.'. The listing's title and organisation terms were matched against the page text first (100% and 100%). This confirms a live page about this programme with a stated high-school or teen audience; it is not a field-by-field audit of cost, grades or dates. | Sept 15: Official page: 'The McDonald's HACER National Scholarship application period is now closed.' The next deadline is not posted (HSO showed 2027-02-05)." },
