  "nyu-tisch": { deadline: null, blurb: "Four-week residential summer conservatory at NYU Tisch with tracks in animation, dance, drama, production and design, dramatic writing, filmmaking, game design, photography and recorded music, earning four to six college credits. Tisch also runs a free 14-week Saturday programme for tri-state students.", verified: true, evidence: "Official page, checked 2026-09-25: the Tisch Summer High School programme is a \"Four-Week Residential Program\" with tracks in Animation, Dance, Drama, Production & Design, Dramatic Writing, Filmmaking, Game Design, Photography and Imaging, and Recorded Music; students earn four to six college credits and the programme is \"tuition-based\". The same page lists a free 14-week Saturday Spring Future Artists Program for tri-state students and online filmmaking and screenwriting workshops worth four credits. No 2027 deadline is posted. | Earlier this run: 2026-09-21 link check: the page returns 200 in a browser; the earlier failure was an incomplete TLS certificate chain that only affects automated fetchers. The high school programmes page is live. | Sept 15: 2026-01-08 was a past cycle's deadline and the official page (checked 2026-09-15) posts no later date." },
  "nywici-scholarship": { deadline: null, category: "Scholarship", evidence: "Official NYWICI page is titled 'Scholarships - NYWICI' with sections '2026 SCHOLARSHIP WINNERS' and 'ELIGIBILITY QUALIFICATIONS'; the programme awards college scholarships to high school seniors and college students in communications. Category corrected from Fellowship to Scholarship. | Sept 15: Official NYWICI page: '2026 SCHOLARSHIP APPLICATION PROGRAM IS NOW CLOSED. The 2027 NYWICI scholarship program will open in the Fall of 2026.' No 2027 deadline posted (HSO showed 2027-01-09)." },
  "o-henry": { deadline: null, opensAt: "2027-03-01", url: "https://www.punoffatx.brushsquaremuseums.org/", title: "O. Henry Pun-Off World Championships", blurb: "Austin wordplay championship with two contests: Punniest of Show, a prepared 90-second routine, and PunSlingers, spontaneous head-to-head rounds. Thirty-two contestants compete in each and places are drawn by lottery, which opens March 1, 2027. There is no separate youth division, so students compete alongside adults.", evidence: "Official site, checked 2026-09-25: punoff.com now redirects to punoffatx.brushsquaremuseums.org, so the austintexas.gov page was a stub. The championship has two contests, \"Punniest of Show\" (prepared 90-second routines) and \"PunSlingers\" (spontaneous rounds), 32 contestants each, held in Austin. The site states \"Mark your calendar for March 1, 2027 when the next lottery opens.\" There is NO youth or junior division anywhere on the official site, so the stored title \"O. Henry Pun-Off Junior\" claimed something the organisers do not offer; retitled to the event that actually exists, which a high schooler may enter through the same lottery. | Sept 15: 2026-05-01 was a past cycle's deadline and the official page (checked 2026-09-15) posts no later date." },
