  "usabo": { deadline: "2026-10-23", blurb: "National biology competition that selects the four-student US team for the International Biology Olympiad, drawing about 12,000 students a year. There are no individual entries: a student's school must register as a host and pay a 125 dollar school fee, so ask a science teacher to register before the deadline.", evidence: "Official page, checked 2026-09-28: 'Schools may register now and pay the registration fee by October 23.' and 'There are no individual registrations.' and 'Each student registers with his/her school ONLY after receiving confirmation from their Test Administrator that his/her school is registered for 2027.' The stored deadline of 2026-11-15 came from the original import, had never been checked, and was over three weeks LATE - a student trusting it would have missed registration. The other October date on the page, October 20, 2026, is the cut-off for schools volunteering to host homeschooled students, not the student deadline. The fee is '$125 registration fee/school', paid by the school rather than the student, so the cost stays Free from a student's point of view and the blurb says who pays. | Sept 15: CEE announcement (August 7, 2026) and the official 'What's new in the 2027 USABO' page: 'The final deadline for both schools and students to complete online registration is November 15, 2026.'" },
