  "usef": { deadline: "2026-10-27", blurb: "Two student leaders from each state, DC and the Department of Defense Education Activity spend Washington Week in D.C. in March and each receive a $12,500 college scholarship. Apply through your state selection contact, not nationally: each state sets its own deadline and most fall in October, so check your state's date now.", category: "Scholarship", verified: true, evidence: "Official state contacts page, checked 2026-09-26: students do not apply nationally, they apply through a state selection contact, and the page lists 52 separate state deadlines running from August 1, 2026 to October 27, 2026 - 40 of them in October and 11 in September. The December 1, 2026 date given elsewhere on the site is the deadline for STATES to submit their chosen delegates, not for students, so recording it would have told students they had two extra months they do not have. The latest state deadline is recorded here and the blurb sends students to their own state's date. Program week is March 6-13, 2027 and each delegate receives a $12,500 college scholarship. | Earlier this run: Official page (ussenateyouth.org), checked 2026-09-21: The national deadline for all states to submit their delegate selections is December 1, 2026. Students apply through their own state education agency rather than to the national programme, so the listing carries no student-facing date; state deadlines are earlier than the December 1 national one. | Earlier this run: Official page (ussenateyouth.org): 'each delegate will also be awarded a $12,500 college scholarship for undergraduate studies' and 'The 65th annual United States Senate Youth Program Washington Week will be in Washington, D.C. March 6 - 13, 2027.' HSO's blurb said $10,000. Students apply through a state selection contact whose deadline varies, so the deadline stays TBA. Category corrected from Fellowship to Scholarship. | Sept 15: Official page: 'Deadlines for application are being updated now and vary by state' (state deadlines fall in Sept-Oct 2026); the 2025-10-15 date is cleared." },
  "usnco": { deadline: null, blurb: "Four-tier national chemistry competition: local exams each March, a national exam in April for more than a thousand nominees, a June study camp for the top twenty, and four places on the US team for the International Chemistry Olympiad. Students register through their ACS local section coordinator, not directly.", evidence: "Official ACS page, checked 2026-09-25: \"a multi-tiered chemistry competition for high school students\" with four tiers - Local Chemistry Olympiad Exams \"held each March\", National Exams \"administered to more than 1,000 students each April\", a June Study Camp for \"The 20 top-scoring students\", and the International Chemistry Olympiad in July where \"four students are chosen to represent the U.S.\". Entry is through a local coordinator: \"Parents and guardians seeking to register students for participation in the 2027 U.S. National Chemistry Olympiad (USNCO) must contact their USNCO Coordinator\". 2027 dates are not yet published. | Sept 15: 2026-03-15 was a past cycle's deadline and the official page (checked 2026-09-15) posts no later date." },
