  "cuny-baruch-college-now-stem-research-academy": { verified: true, evidence: "Official page fetched and corroborated 2026-09-26 (HTTP 200). Eligibility wording on the page: 'Student Resources Contact Us STEM Research Academy The Baruch College Now STEM Research Academy is designed to provide NYC public high school students with an opportunity to build their science knowledge and skills by engaging in ‘authentic inquiry’ activities.'. The page also describes the programme: 'Students selected are enrolled in a college-credit research methods course during the spring to strengthen necessary skills, such as formulating a strong research question, designing testable experiments, performing literature searches, and reading scientific literature.'. 100% of the listing's title terms and 100% of its organisation terms appear in the page text. This confirms the link resolves to a live page about this programme that is open to high schoolers. It is not a field-by-field audit of cost, grades or dates. | Earlier this run: 2026-09-21 link check: the whole collegenow.baruch.cuny.edu host, including its home page, returns HTTP 500 with the message Database Error. That is a server outage rather than a moved or retired page, so the listing is left as it is and flagged here for a re-check on the next pass." },
  "roswell-park-comprehensive-cancer-center-high-school-summer-rese": { opensAt: "2026-10-01", blurb: "Summer laboratory placement at Roswell Park, the only NCI-designated comprehensive cancer centre in upstate New York, running June 28 to August 6, 2027. Open only to juniors enrolled in Erie, Niagara, Cattaraugus or Chautauqua county; it is commuter-based and there is no application fee.", verified: true, evidence: "Official page, checked 2026-09-22: Program dates: June 28-August 6, 2027. The application portal will open in the beginning of October. All high school juniors enrolled in school in Erie, Niagara, Cattaraugus or Chautauqua county are encouraged to apply; applications from students enrolled outside these counties will not be considered. Enrolled in junior year (graduating class of 2028). This is a commuter-based only program, there are no exceptions. There are no application fees." },
  "university-of-texas-at-austin-summer-high-school-research-academ": { opensAt: "2027-01-04", verified: true, evidence: "Official page, checked 2026-09-22: HSRA Application will open again January 2027. The closed cycle shows Application Deadline: March 22, 2026, and Full Tuition Due: May 15. WE DO NOT PROVIDE HOUSING OR TRANSPORTATION - accepted participants must make their own housing and transportation arrangements." },
  "memorial-sloan-kettering-cancer-center-summer-student-program": { opensAt: "2026-12-01", blurb: "Eight-week laboratory placement at Memorial Sloan Kettering for high school students interested in biomedical science. Applicants must live in New York, New Jersey or Connecticut within 25 miles of the Upper East Side main campus. Students receive a 1,200 dollar stipend; housing is not provided.", verified: true, evidence: "Official page, checked 2026-09-22: Founded in 2010, the Summer Student Program is designed for high school students who are interested in pursuing careers in the biomedical sciences. Demographic eligibility: The applicant must live in New York, New Jersey, or Connecticut within 25 miles of Main Campus of Memorial Sloan Kettering Cancer Center on the Upper East Side in Manhattan. Students receive a stipend of 1,200 dollars for the summer. Housing is not provided. Applications open on December 1." },
  "the-wistar-institute-high-school-program-in-biomedical-research": { blurb: "Four-week summer fellowship at the Wistar Institute in University City for fifteen students, learning laboratory technique in Wistar's training lab and contributing to live projects. No prior research experience is needed. Students receive SEPTA passes and a 1,500 dollar stipend on completion.", verified: true, evidence: "Official page, checked 2026-09-22: Students spend four weeks over the summer learning best-practices in biomedical laboratory techniques while also contributing to active Wistar science projects in their state-of-the-science Training Lab. The program supports 15 highly-motivated high school students. No prior research experience is necessary. Students from Philadelphia high schools are strongly encouraged to apply. Students will receive SEPTA passes to defray the cost of traveling to and from the Institute. A stipend of 1,500 dollars will be awarded for successful completion. Our 2026 High School Program has concluded, so the listing keeps Deadline TBA." },
  "forsyth-institute-forsyth-student-scholars-summer-internship-pro": { deadline: "2027-04-01", url: "https://forsyth.org/forsyth-student-scholars-summer-program/", blurb: "Paid summer research internship at the ADA Forsyth Institute for local high school students, 35 hours a week at minimum wage, working on oral and craniofacial science alongside Forsyth researchers. Applications close on April 1 each year.", verified: true, evidence: "URL repointed to the summer-programme page, which carries the dates; checked 2026-09-22: ADA Forsyth Student Scholars opens doors to careers in STEM for local high school students. High School Summer Internship. Salary (minimum wage), 35 hours per week. Application deadline: April 1. The date is stated without a year as the programme's standing annual deadline, so the listing carries the next one." },
  "uchicago-medicine-chicago-eyes-on-cancer-program": { verified: true, evidence: "2026-09-22 re-check: the listing's URL sits under the UChicago Medicine Comprehensive Cancer Center's Pathway Programs for High School and Undergraduate Students section, which is live and lists the cancer centre's high school pathway programmes including Chicago EYES on Cancer." },
